                    <ref target="frus1946v11#pg_105">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1946, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">xi</hi>, p. 105</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d100-f2" n="23" xml:id="d100-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1942v06#pg_443">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.</hi>, 1942, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >vi</hi>, p. 443</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d100-f3" n="24" xml:id="d100-f3-content">
                <p>The Secretary of War replied in a memorandum of May 29 that the War Department
                    would abide by the objections raised by the Department of State in the above
                    letter (810.7962/5–2947).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
